  "asked": "Headless build in Brett's AmberX-AXF repo (this worktree, branch claude/urgent-builds). Opus, one session, no sub-agents. Brett gave GO (Oct 31 morning, again tonight 7:30 PM): do the whole URGENT profile now, it is FIRST. Load first: CLAUDE.md, _claude/shared/rules/RULES.md, and the spec from axHub: mcp__claude_ai_axHub__call (or mcp__axHub__call) tool axhub.memory_read {project:'amberx-axf', area:'data', path:'framework/plan/specs/prompt-profiles-and-queue-reconciler.md'}. Read ALL of it, esp. 'GO GIVEN' at the bottom. Check branch origin/fable/split-steps for prior work and reuse it. Order: 1. MASTER CLEANUP: one Orchestrator-owned builds store (profiles are a field, not separate copies), one Builds plugin, every write versioned, remove Console init regenerate-from-plan. Dry-run migration report FIRST (_claude/builds/reports/urgent-migration-dryrun.md), keep old files read-only one release. Nothing lost: every build, step, status, note from every profile + Pending list ends up in the store. 2. STEPS VIEW: atomic steps as versioned records; drag to reorder steps AND builds; multi-select; divide a step further; harvest + split-into-N; Restore default; draft until Apply, Discard. RENAME builds, steps and profiles (double-tap/double-click name or right-click/long-press > Rename; inline; Enter saves, Esc cancels; empty refused; id never changes so links/PRs/history hold; every view shows the new title). 3. LIVE PROGRESS BARS per build and profile. Register the build in the orchestrator under profile 'urgent' first. Framework controls + theme/scale tokens only (asset-conformant), web + AmberX. Tests for migration (no data lost), reorder, rename, apply/discard. Run the full local test block from .github/workflows/android.yml + theme/controls/lifecycle checks; all green. Commit per step. git fetch origin && git merge origin/main; retest; git push origin HEAD:main, retry until it lands; push the branch too. Detailed report (file touched, what was wrong, before